title: the activity log is written only by pick, so karr log and context are near-empty
updated: 2026-08-10T01:27:58Z
---

`grep -rn append_log lib/` finds exactly one call site: `Cmd/Pick.pm:173`. So
the activity log is written by `pick` and by nothing else:

    karr create a; karr move 1 todo; karr edit 1 -a note; karr archive 1
    karr log   -> "No log entries."
    karr pick --claim tester --move in-progress
    karr log   -> 1 entry, the only one karr ever writes

kanban-md logs from create, move, edit, delete, archive, handoff, pick and
block/unblock/claim/release — 16 call sites via `cmd/root.go:168`.

This matters beyond `karr log`: `karr show --me/--agent/--last` and `karr context`
read the same log, so the agent-facing history surfaces are working off
near-empty data and quietly look "correct". `karr backup` does not include
`refs/karr/log/*` either, so what little exists is not in snapshots.

Fix: log from every mutating command (one shared helper, not 8 copies), and
include the log refs in backup/restore.
Fixed and merged into main; full suite green at 88 files / 566 tests.

Every one of these was reproduced before it was fixed and left a regression test
that was verified to fail against the pre-fix code -- not a test that merely
passes now. Details and what was deliberately NOT fixed are in the merge commit
that names this ticket.
